* Regarding PTM implementation:
 It makes the base score batch-relative, which the findings doc already
 flags as the reason the tail is fitted rather than pure-rank. Today a
 segment's contribution depends only on the index; afterwards it depends
 on the letter bag, because the bag determines the class list. Two
 consequences: scores stop being comparable across puzzles, and rerank-
 anagrams — which revalidates an old result file by rebuilding a prepared
 class list and rescoring through dfs_representative_upper_log_score
 (rerank-anagrams.cpp:332) — only reproduces the original numbers if it
 reconstructs an identical fit. If the bag or the dictionary shifted at
 all, old score columns silently stop matching.

 Fitting over the whole index instead of the class list would remove that
 entirely and make the map a property of the index, at the cost of a
 one-time scan (or a summary stored alongside the index). If this is
 headed anywhere, that's the version I'd argue for.

